    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">smegma</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">smigma</span></b> 
		and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zmeg-ma</span></b> ),
			ătis (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>dat. plur.</i> smegmatis, <i><span class="en">Plin. 31, 7,
				42, § 92</span></i>), n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμῆγμα</span>, <i>a cleansing
				medicine</i>, <i>a detergent</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				25, 74, § 156</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34, 13, 36, §
			134</span></i>.—For making the skin smooth, <i><span class="en">Plin. 24, 7,
				28, § 43</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Becker, Gallus, 3, p. 64 (2d edit.): afferte
					mihi smigmata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Dan. 13, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
